Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 54 CLINICAL DATA  History of invasive DCA                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SINGLE MICROSCOPIC FOCUS ABOUT REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MEDIAL MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Invasion of the stroma  blood vessels  and lymphatic vessels is not seen  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION  METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA IN 1 OF 20 LYMPH NODES AND EXTENDING TO THE AXILLARY SOFT TISSUE  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA  ADDITIONAL    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 5 OF 5 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 54                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Lymph node  left Axilla   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 58 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are 3 specimens  Labeled  left breast lump  short stitch superior  long stitch lateral  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm fragment of breast tissue with 2 stitches and a REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm skin ellipse  The specimen is inked entirely in black  the superior half is overlaid with blue  sectioned to reveal an ill defined  firm  tan white nodule  3 0cm in longest dimension  extending to the superior  posterior and lateral resection margins  Representative sections are submitted from medial to lateral in cassettes A through H   A and H are themost medial and lateral sections respectively  C and D one mass in realtionship to the posterior margin  E and F tumor in relationship to the superior margin   Labeled  left axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm fibroadipose tissue  Numerous lymph nodes are dissected  ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 3 0cm in largest diameter  The largest lymph node has a tan white yellow  homogeneous and fleshy cut surface  Representative sections of the largest lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes I and J  Representative sections of the remaining lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes K through O  Labeled  additional axillary tissue  are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  The lymph nodes are dissected and submitted entirely in cassette P  Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REP