Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 22 CLINICAL DATA  43 year old female with right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST   RIGHT BREAST 11 O CLOCK  1    NEEDLE CORE BIOPSIES  BIPHASIC NEOPLASM WITH INCREASED STROMAL CELLULARITY AND MITOTIC ACTIVITY   SEE NOTE   BREAST   RIGHT BREAST  11 O CLOCK  2    BIOPSIES  CONSISTENT WITH FOCALLY INFARCTED FIBROADENOMA  NOTE  The tumor is a biphasic tumor in which there is increased stromal cellularity and stromal mitotic activity  The differential includes cellular fibroadenoma and phyllodes tumor  The nature of the core biopsy limits optimal architectural assessment of the neoplasm  Thus  the distinction between a cellular fibroadenoma and a phyllodes tumor cannot be accurately ascertained  Excision is recommended to best evaluate the lesion  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 05                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast 11 o clock  1   are 7 cores of soft  tan tissue  ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm which are submitted in toto as Cassette A  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast 11 o clock  2   are 8 cores of soft  tan tissue  ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm which are submitted in toto as Cassette B  Gross Description by  Robert F Donnell Resident  IVANA DELALLE  MD  PHD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Edwin Clyde