esult was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 09 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Deep margin  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of white to tan fibroadipose tissue  submitted entirely in A  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast lesion  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with localizing wire in place  A roentgenogram accompanies this specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a firm  irregular lesion  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm in greatest dimension  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  The remainder of the tissue is submitted entirely in B through L  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST LESION   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Kathleen O Neil Smith  BUMS O R  Diagnosis by  Asif Rashid  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY PART B  DEEP MARGIN  LEFT BREAST    report_end  , Unchecked.
