e tissue  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted in cassettes C L from medial to lateral orientation  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast inferior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm piece of white fibrous tissue with some attached yellow adipose tissue and a long stitch marking the true margin  The true margin is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned entirely submitted in cassettes M and N  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast medial margin  is a piece of tan white fibrous tissue with attached tan yellow fat and a stitch marking the true margin  The specimen measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  The margin is inked black and the specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes O and P  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast superior margin  are two fragments of white fibrous tissue with attached fat measuring in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  Each fragment has a black stitch marking the true margin  The true margins are inked black and the specimens are entirely submitted in cassette Q  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast lateral margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm piece of tan white fibrous tissue with a stitch marking the true margin  The margin is inked black  and the specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes R and S  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast anterior margin  are four fragments of tan white fibrous tissue with attached tan yellow fat measuring in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  The specimens are unoriented and are entirely submitted in cassette T  Resident  STEWART M  KNOEPP  MD   Ph D                                                                              