receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 49     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Left   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 23 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a 5 x 4 x 1 5cm piece of unoriented breast tissue with a needle localization wire  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an irregular  tan white  sclerotic tumor of about 1 2cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections of the unoriented specimen are submitted  The tumor is submitted in cassettes A through D and representative sections of the breast tissue away from the tumor in cassettes E and F  Resident  RICHARD AMMER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS   LEFT BREAST   SUSPICIOUS INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  ABUTTING THE MARGIN  O R  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
