t  Right  block A   The in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  No invasive tumor is present in these sections  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 16 26 Consulting Pathologist s   MELINDA J  FAN  MD GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm unoriented irregular portion of tan pink to yellow fibrofatty tissue with a localizing wire and clip in place  The specimen is accompanied by a radiograph  The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal a dense white fibrotic cut surface with no discrete masses or lesions identified  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes A J  with the area denoted by the clip in cassettes A C  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  anterior superior final shaved margin right breast  are two irregular  unoriented tan pink to yellow rubbery portions of fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The specimens are serially sectioned to reveal a predominately dense white fibrotic cut surface with a minute amount of tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue  No discrete masses or lesions are identified  The specimen is entirely submitted with the smaller portion in cassette K and the larger portion in cassette L M  Received in formalin   l