  with a well healed linear scar measuring 1 6cm  The resection margin is inked black and the specimen is submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast biopsy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm portion of shaggy pink yellow fibroadipose tissue with a long stitch designating lateral and a short stitch superior  The lateral aspect of the specimen shows some cautery artifact  The specimen is inked per protocol with respect to the superior inferior long axis as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  medial green  and lateral yellow  Serial sectioning reveals a gray white ill defined hard mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  grossly abutting the lateral and posterior margins  The mass comes to 0 5cm of the medial margin  and 1cm of the anterior margin  The entire mass is submitted from superior to inferior in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the superior most portion of specimen in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   whole sections in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   partial sections in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and entire bisected portions in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   An inferior section that appears to contain a lymph node is submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast new medial margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1 2cm portion of tan pink shaggy fibroadipose tissue with a suture indicating the new margin  which is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a pink tan yellow fibrofatty cut surface with focal hemorrhage  No discrete masses are identified  The specimen is submitted entirely from one end to the other in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right sentinel node   is a 3 x 2 x 0 4cm piece of fatty tissue containing a single lymph node  The lymph node is frozen entirely FX 1  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remaining portion of the specimen is submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary sentinel node   is a 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of soft tissue containing a lymph node which is dissected free and frozen entirely as FX 2  now resubmitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remainder of the specimen is submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1  RIGHT SENTINEL NODE  BLUE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE  130   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Gross Dictation by Matthew M Johnson M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Matthew M Johnson M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  SKIN  RIGHT BREAST   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  RIGHT MEDIAL MARGIN   EXCISION PART D  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION PART E  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION PART F  CRYOSTAT FROZEN SECTION  SLIDE ONLY  PART G  CRYOSTAT FROZEN SECTION  SLI , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  23 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 59 CLINICAL DATA                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE LATERAL AND ANTERIOR MARGINS   SEE NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  ASSOCIATED WITH THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  AND PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE ANTERIOR AND LATERAL MARGINS  NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR MEDIAL MARGIN    EXCISION  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  RADIAL SCARS  MICROSCOPIC  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGINS    EXCISION  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION  ALL  14  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  BREAST  RIGHT  RE EXCISION   INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FOCALLY ATYPICAL  WITH ASSOCIATED MICROCALCIFICATIONS  PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE SUPERIOR MARGIN  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL INVASIVE CARCINOMA  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION  ALL  14  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  LYMPH NODE   ADDITIONAL RIGHT AXILLA    EXCISION  ONE LYMPH NODE IS FREE OF CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 36                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 12 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Seven specimens are received  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast biopsy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm incision of breast biopsy with long suture designating lateral and short suture designating superior aspect  The specimen is inked as follows  Inferior is yellow  superior is red  lateral is blue  medial is green  anterior and posterior are black  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm stellate gritty mass present at the anterior margin and 0 2cm from the posterior margin  0 5cm from the lateral margin  Mass is submitted in cassettes A through C with anterior  black   lateral  blue   and posterior  black overinked in yellow   Needle localization site  slightly firm no gross tumor  and anterior margin are submitted in D  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are the 6 remaining specimens  Labeled as  left breast  additional anterior medial margin  is an unoriented portion of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibroadipose tissue with focal fibrocystic changes  submitted entirely in cassettes E through J  Labeled as  left breast  final shaved margins  are three fragments of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm in aggregate  They are inked and sectioned to reveal fibroadipose tissue with focal cystic changes  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes K  L and M  Labeled as  left axillary contents  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of adipose tissue from which multiple lymph nodes are extracted  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 7cm in greatest dimension  submitted in N through S  Labeled as  reexcision  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm skin ellipse containing a 4 8cm well healed  linear scar  There is a long stitch designating the lateral aspect  and a short stitch designating the superior aspect which is inked in blue  while the inferior aspect is inked in black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm biopsy cavity with an associated area of stellate fibrosis measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm and extending to the superior and inferior margins  Posterior to the biopsy cavity is a rubbery  tan white  nodular mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm and present at superior  inferior and posterior margins  The biopsy cavity itself is 0 2cm from the nearest  inferior  margin  Section code  T W  Biopsy cavity  nearest margin in W  lateral to medial X Y  Adjacent fibrous areas Z  Uninvolved parenchyma Designated right axillary contents is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of adipose tissue from which several node like structures have been extracted ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm in greatest dimension and submitted in cassettes AA through DD  Labeled as  additional axillary tissue  right  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of adipose tissue from which several node like structures have been extracted ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm in greatest dimension submitted entirely in cassette EE  Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION PART D  LYMPH NODES   ADDITIONAL RIGHT AXILLA    EXCISION PART E  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION PART F  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR MARGIN    EZXCIS PART G  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGINS    EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  CorrectedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 REMOVED_MONTH 00 ACCESSIONED ON  01 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 11 39 CLINICAL DATA  52 y o  female with new density right breast UOQ SCB  carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  BREAST  RIGHT 2   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Jacqueline Haas  MD Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 17 21                                                                                     BREAST CANCER IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY ADDENDUM Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   Both Specimens  The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Please see the report for specimen  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   which states that both tumors show strong overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  The lack of overexpression in the current specimens probably represents falsely negative determinations arising from methodological effects  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 08 46    REVISED REMOVED_DATE    GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right UOQ SCB  are seven cores of tan yellow fibrofatty tissue ranging in size from 0 5cm to 2 0cm which are submitted in toto as cassette A  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  are four cores of tan yellow fibrofatty tissue ranging in size from 0 5cm to 0 8cm which are submitted in toto to cassette B  Gross Description by  TARA HARRIS Resident  JOHN BISSONNETTE  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Heather Aliotta  NP Michele Gryzenia Ramsdell  M D  Eren D Yeh  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSIES PART B  BREAST  RIGHT  2   CORE BIOPSIES , Unchecked.
