neath the nipple and areola is nodular  The rest of the breast parenchyma contains a tan yellow lobulated cut surface interspersed with scant fibrous tissue and occasional cyst filled with blue fluid consistent with fibrocystic changes  No additional discrete mass or lesion is noted  No lymph nodes are grossly appreciated in the upper outer  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire first ill defined mass to include the posterior inked margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire second mass to include the posterior inked margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  fibrous breast parenchyma between first and second mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  nodular breast parenchyma  central quadrant  previously inked blue    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  fibrous breast tissue  upper outer quadrant  Received in one additional container  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  Real  REMOVE_MRN and  additional mastectomy skin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm aggregate of tan red fibrofatty tissue partially surfaced by roughly triangular portions of tan pink skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  Sectioning reveals no gross abnormalities  and representative sections are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1 AND 1A  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is ass