Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 27 CLINICAL DATA  Fifty five year old female now undergoing right breast needle localization  lumpectomy  and axillary node dissection  Invasive carcinoma on previous core biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISION OF CORE BIOPSY SITE  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  90    REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE 2 OF 3  EXTENDING TO A MARGIN  POSTEROLATERAL   THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  SEE NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  10    INTERMEDIATE GRADE  CRIBRIFORM TYPE WITH NECROSIS  CONFINED TO THE REGION OF INVASIVE TUMOR  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS  WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND FLORID DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  HEALING CORE BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  No lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is identified  BREAST  RIGHT   NEW SUPERIOR MARGIN    BIOPSY  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT   NEW DEEP MARGIN    BIOPSY  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT   NEW MEDIAL MARGIN    BIOPSY  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT   NEW LATERAL MARGIN    BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT   NEW INFERIOR MARGIN    BIOPSY  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   REGIONAL DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 19 of 19 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 45                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 28 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fibroadipose tissue fragment with a localization wire  The specimen is inked black and the lateral half is over inked green  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm ill defined  firm area abutting the posterolateral resection margin  A representative section of the firm area is frozen as FX  1  and resubmitted in A  The remaining firm area is submitted entirely in B E from superior to inferior  Additional representative sections are submitted in F H  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  new superior margin  suture on true margin    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue with a stitch on one side  The site of the stitch is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes I and J  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  new deep margin  suture on true margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm fragment of adipose tissue with a suture denoting the true margin  This margin is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned  and submitted entirely in cassettes K and L  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  new medial margin  suture on true margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm fragment of adipose tissue with a suture  Site of the suture is inked black and over inked orange  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes M and N  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  new lateral margin  suture on true margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fragment of adipose tissue with a stitch on the true margin which is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes O and P  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  new inferior margin  suture on true margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm fragment of adipose tissue with a suture on the true margin  This margin is inked black and the specimen serially sectioned  submitted entirely in cassettes Q and R  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm aggregate of adipose tissue  A lymph node dissection is performed with lymph nodes submitted in cassettes S AA  Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT  POSTEROLATERAL MARGIN   INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA PRESENT AT THE POSTEROLATERAL MARGIN  O R  Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD O R  Diag