w strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   30  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Friday REMOVED_MONTH 16   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 12 26 24PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  2  RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Left  Posterior Medial  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Amplified   See note  Note  The microinvasive tumor cells are not reliably identified on the slide examined by HER 2 FISH  Signal counts were obtained from the ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells  which also show HER 2 protein overexpression  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  826  to chromosome 17 signals  99  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  The results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be interpreted with caution  Equivocal Amplification   Reference  Journal of Clinical Oncology 25 118 145   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Addendum  2 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 21   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 03 36 18PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed thi