ith no other masses or other gross abnormalities  Sectioning of the axillary tail reveals numerous tan pink lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 2 1cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A B  Tumor to deep margin  C D  Tumor to superficial margin  E F  Representatives fibrous tissue away from tumor  G M  Lymph nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  additional superficial tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm aggregate of irregular tan pink fibroadipose tissue fragments with no orientation  The fragments are serially sectioned and entirely submitted as N P  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  additional axillary tissue  are two grey pink lymph nodes  a REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm in greatest dimension  with minimal attached tan yellow adipose tissue  The lymph nodes are submitted in toto as Q  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  umbilical hernia  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm irregular portion of grey white to tan pink fibromembranous fibroadipose tissue which is serially sectioned to reveal no areas of induration or other gross abnormalities  Representative sections are submitted as R  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  RESIDENT FREE SERVICE  FCK                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Jonathan Michael Winograd  M D  PART A  BREAST LEFT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST LEFT ADDITIONAL SUPERFICIAL TISSUE  EXCISIO PART C  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA  ADDITIONAL   EXCISION PART D  HERINA SAC UMBILICAL  EXCISION , Unchecked.
