nd  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fibrofatty breast tissue with short suture indicating superior margin  long suture indicating lateral margin  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm tan pink  hard nodule that is located at 0 1cm from the posterior  0 4cm from the superior  0 6cm from the anterior and 2 5cm from the inferior margin  A 0 1cm firm nodule is located 0 2cm from the posterior margin and is frozen as fx  1  and submitted as I and a 0 2cm firm nodule located  0 2cm from the anterior margin is submitted as J  The lateral margin is submitted en face in K and the superior margin is submitted in L  The rest of the specimen is submitted from lateral to medial in cassettes M Y  Resident  ARASH RADFAR  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  SOHEIL DADRAS  MD  PHD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST RIGHT FINAL SHAVED MARGIN  PART C  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY  SENTINEL   BIOPSY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 55 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  INVOLVING 14 OF 20 BLOCKS AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  RADIAL SCAR  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The carcinoma in situ involves a pre existing benign sclerosing nodule as well as ducts and lobules throughout the specimen  The architecture of the benign nodules makes evaluation of invasion difficult in this focus  Convincing stromal invasion is not seen  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 MAY 98 at 14 08                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 MAY 98 at 15 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a 6 x 5 x 2cm piece of breast  inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm well demarcated  tan nodule  adjacent to the inked margin  The remainder of the tissue is mostly fatty with focal fibrous areas  The nodule submitted entirely in cassettes A and B with representative sections of more fibrous areas of the breast in cassettes C through J and Q Z  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x 5 x 2cm piece of breast  inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 2cm tan  firm mass extending to within 0 1cm from the nearest inked resection margin  The remainder of the breast tissue is grossly unremarkable  A section of the mass in relation to the inked margin is frozen as FX  1  now in cassette K  Additional sections of the mass are submitted in cassettes L through O with representative section of adjacent breast tissue in cassette P  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  NO AREA SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM TO THE RESECTION MARGIN  O R  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  H  Thomas Aretz  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  David L Berger  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
