VE_PATIENT_NAME  Preston  REMOVE_MRN  only  are four cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm which are submitted in toto as cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Also received in the same container is a blue cassette  opened to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm fibrofatty tissue core which is submitted in toto as cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  The invasive and invasive and ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells show similar estrogen  and progesterone receptor expression  The invasive tumor cells are negative for HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with moderate  2   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2 in the ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  The tumor cell membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   over overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics d