Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  01 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 51 CLINICAL DATA  Breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   LUMPECTOMY  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  PRESENT ADJACENT TO AND EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE AND AT INKED SURFACES ALONG A BROAD FRONT  SEE NOTE   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  NOTE  Definite residual invasive carcinoma is not seen  The residual DCIS spans at least 1 4cm  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY   METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 2 OF 14 LYMPH NODES  BOTH OF WHICH DISPLAY PROMINENT EXTRANODAL SOFT TISSUE EXTENSION  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 48                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm piece of fibroadipose breast tissue  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm skin ellipse with a 5 0cm well healed incision site  located centrally  The unoriented specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm hemorrhagic biopsy cavity containing serosangineous fluid  The biopsy cavity comes within 0 2cm of the closest margin  deep   The parenchyma surrounding the biopsy cavity has focal areas of fibrosis and cystic areas surrounding the cavity  ranging to REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm in greatest dimension  The remaining parenchyma is sectioned to reveal multiple microcysts and prominent vessels  and is without additional discrete lesions  SECTION CODE  A   Biopsy cavity in relation to deep margin  B   Biopsy cavity in relation to skin  C   Biopsy cavity in relation to cystic structures  D   Biopsy cavity with hemorrhagic areas  E   Representative section from adjacent  unremarkable parenchymal area  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm portion of adipose tissue  from which multiple lymph nodes are identified  ranging from 0 5cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  A representative section from each lymph node is submitted in Cassettes F L  Note that representative sections of the largest lymph node is bisected and submitted entirely in cassettes K L  Resident  SAMANTHA J  PULLIAM  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Rosa Sung Eun Choi  M D  David L Berger  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   LUMPECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  04 AUG 98 ACCESSIONED ON  04 AUG 98 at 13 19 CLINICAL DATA  Previous history right breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  REMOVED_DATE CM   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The tumor is focally less than 0 1cm from an inked margin  Vascular or lymphatic invasion are not seen  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  06 AUG 98 at 19 15                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 AUG 98 at 13 43 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of fibroadipose tissue which is unoriented  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal an ill defined  firm white  focally cystic area which is entirely submitted in cassette A  The remainder of the specimen is grossly unremarkable and is entirely submitted in cassette B  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  SELIM NASSER  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
