ions of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast with some axillary contents  is a right modified radical mastectomy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm  There is an overlying skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm with a 3 0cm curved healed incision 3 0cm lateral to the unremarkable nipple  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm firm tan white mass with areas of white streaking and a granular gritty cut surface  approximately 1 6cm inferior to the incision and extending to 0 5cm of the deep inked margin  Approximately 4 0cm medial to the lesion is a firm white area approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  grossly abutting the inked deep margin  The remainder of the parenchyma shows foci of firm white gritty tissue within areas of gray fibrous soft tissue  These areas 