Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  27 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 20 CLINICAL DATA  64 year old female status post a left  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  breast cancer in  REMOVED_CASE_ID   who now presents with two suspicious areas on mammogram of the right breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  1   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  95    MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3  AND LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  5    WITH PAGETOID SPREAD INTO DUCTS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor measures 1 7cm in greatest dimension on histologic section  slide A  and extends to the inked resection margin  The carcinoma infiltrates insidiously throughout much of the specimen  No definite vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  2  MILD INTRADUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA WITH FOCAL APOCRINE METAPLASIA  BREAST  RIGHT  2   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  90    MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED   GRADE 2 3   AND LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  10   WITH PAGETOID SPREAD INTO DUCTS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor measures 1 3cm in greatest dimension on histologic section  slide J   and extends to within 0 1cm of the inked resection margin  No difinite vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  2  SEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  3  INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMAS  4  MILD FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 50                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT  BOTH NODULES   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 26 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two separate parts  Labeled  Right breast   1  is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 2cm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue  with needle localizing wire in place  and accompanying specimen x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a tan  firm mass with ill defined borders  that extends to the inked resection margin  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  The remainder of the specimen is submitted entirely in A through F  with the tumor mass in A through C  Labeled  Right breast  2  is a 3 x 2 x 2cm 