Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2 Results To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D  Signed Out by  Melinda J Lerwill  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  Left mastectomy with stitch at 12 o clock  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  MULTICENTRIC INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SEE TABLE  1  2  EXTENSIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   4  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  At least 4 foci  measuring 0 7cm  0 6cm  0 15cm  and  0 1cm  located in the lower outer  anterolateral  upper inner  and central inferior regions of the breast  respectively  See note  GRADE  1  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Indeterminate  See note  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Invasive carcinoma extends to  0 1cm from the anterior margin in one focus in the lateral breast  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within and beyond the region of the invasive carcinoma  present in multiple quadrants  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  1 to focal 2  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Positive at the anterior margin of the specimen in the lower outer quadrant  Ductal carcinoma in situ is also  0 1cm from the anterior margin in several other foci in the lateral breast and the central inferior breast  and comes to 0 17cm from the posterior margin in one focus in the lower outer quadrant  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NOTE  Additional foci of early invasive papillary carcinoma cannot be entirely excluded in regions of myoepithelial cell loss associated with ductal carcinoma in situ  immunostains