lue of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  05 MAY 94 at 11 23 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm piece of fatty soft tissue  with a localizing wire in place  An x ray accompanies this specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal several REMOVED_DATE to 0 3cm firm  tan nodules  The entire specimen is submitted in A through J  with nodules in A through C  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  SEVERAL SMALL  0 1 0 3 CM  NODULES  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS TO ASSESS THE POSSIBILITY OF CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Karen C  Deering  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
