Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 36 CLINICAL DATA  50 year old female with left breast mass and positive FNA for cancer  Chest x ray  LFT s and bone scan negative  Negative family history for breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  EXTENSIVE  SEE NOTE   2  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  UNEQUIVOCAL METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 14 OF 16 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Tumor is present in sections from the main mass  the satellite mass  1 4cm inferior to the main mass   random sections from the medial and lateral breast and tissue subjacent to the nipple  The multifocal nature of the carcinoma precludes an accurate assessment tumor size  The largest single tumor mass is REMOVED_DATE x 4 0x 3 0cm  Margins appear free of tumor  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  LYMPH NODES   ADDITIONAL AXILLARY TISSUE    METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 6 OF 6 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 20                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 37 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in two parts each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  Labeled  left modified mastectomy  is a 17 x 10cm ellipse of skin with an eccentrically placed normal appearing nipple overlying a 23 x 15 x 4cm mass of breast tissue with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail at one end  Black suture is present on one edge of the specimen  superior   The epidermal surface shows areas of hyperpigmentation  however  no scar is grossly identified  Sectioning into the specimen shows a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm cylindrical mass present 2 0cm deep to the epidermis  2 0cm anterior to the deep margin  4 0cm from the inferior margin  6 0cm from the superior margin  15 0cm from the lateral margin  and approximately 7 0cm from the medial margin  On closer inspection  the mass is composed of dense fibrous tissue enveloping areas of more normal appearing fibroadipose tissue causing focal retraction and puckering  1 5cm inferior to this area there is a second 2 0cm in diameter area of gritty  white tissue which is 1 0cm from the closest margin  SECTION CODE A B  Representative sections of deep margin  closer approach in B   C D  Representative sections of tumor mass  E F  Representative random sections of normal breast parenchyma  medial and lateral  G  Representative sections of nipple  H  Representative sections of satellie  1 5cm inferior to the main tumor mass  I  One lymph node bisected  J  Two lymph nodes bisected  K  Two lymph nodes bisected  L  Three lymph nodes  M  Two lymph nodes bisected  N  Two lymph nodes bisected  O  One lymph node trisected  P  Two lymph nodes bisected  Q  One large firm lymph node bisected  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional axillary tissue  are six small irregular nodules of fibroadipose tissue lymph nodes  entirely in R  Resident  Robin E  Kirby  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Irene Kuter  M D  Claire Y Fung  M D  PART A  BREAST PART B  AXILLA   report_end  , Unchecked.
