Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 53 CLINICAL DATA  Excisional biopsy of the right breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE II III   PRESENT AT MULTIPLE INKED MARGINS WITH FOCI SUSPICIOUS FOR LYMPHATIC INVASION   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENSIVE  MIXED LOW AND INTERMEDIATE GRADE  WITH ASSOCIATED MICROCALCIFICATIONS  PRESENT AT SEVERAL INKED SURFACES  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 22 08                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 05 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm segment of fibrofatty breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal an irregular 2 5cm firm tan white mass  which is 0 1cm from the closest inked margin  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1 and frozen section  2  The remainder is submitted entirely in cassettes A through G  Frozen section  1 submitted as H  and frozen section  2 is submitted in cassette I  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  O R  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
