mone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 56 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue  The tissue was inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm firm tan nodule that abuts an inked margin  The lesion s radiograph is enclosed  Representative sections were saved as frozen section  1  Representative sections of the remaining tissue are submitted in cassettes A through J  Section Code  A F  firm nodule  G I  portions of white hard tissue  J  unremarkable tissue  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  COLLOID CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
